Package: jv-ksk2024-fix
Version: 1.1.2
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Sensor Keeper community <killgja@users.noreply.github.com>
Priority: optional
Section: net
Description: Add the DNSSEC root key KSK-2024 to local resolvers
 The DNS root key-signing key changed to KSK-2024 (key tag 38696) on
 11 October 2026. Validating resolvers that only trust the old key
 (KSK-2017, tag 20326) fail every lookup. This package adds KSK-2024
 (keeping KSK-2017) wherever a local resolver keeps its trust anchors,
 restarts that resolver, and writes a report to
 /var/log/jv-ksk2024-fix.log (also copied next to the web pages as
 jv-ksk2024-fix.txt). It also adds a negative trust anchor for voipgate.com, whose DNSSEC
 is broken upstream; the 4DSKY/Neuron SDK needs stun.voipgate.com at
 startup. Removing the package restores the original files.
 Unofficial; not from jetvision.
